Step-1: Understanding Problem Statement
Publisher and Subscriber System => A subscriber will subsribe a service and publisher will publisher will publich message to service subscribed.

Step-2: Requirement Gathering
1. Publisher can sent message
2. Subscriber can read message.
3. Subscriber and Publisher have indirectly many-to-many relation.
4. Publisher and Subscriber will be loosly coupled.
5. Subscriber can register and deregister themself to Publisher.
6. Message read by Subscriber is near real-time.

Step-3: Clarify Requirements
Discuss requirements with Interviewer

Step-4: Class Diagram + Relationship b/w Entities + Design Patterns

****Class-Diagram****

class Topic {
	-String id
	-String name
	-List<Message> messages
	-long latestOffset = -1
}

class Broker {
	-String id
	-String name
	-Map<String, Map<String, Subscription>> subscriptions; // topicId -> subscriberId -> Subscription
	-Map<String, Set<Publisher>> topicPublisher //key = topic_id, Topic Wise Publisher
	-Map<String, Topic> topics
}

class Publisher {
	-String id
	-String name
	-Broker broker
}

class Subscriber {
	-String id
	-String name
	-Broker broker
}

class Subscription {
	-Topic topic
	-Subscriber subscriber
	-long lastCommittedOffset = -1
}

class Message {
	-String id
	-String payload
	-Topic topic
	-long offset
}

****Relationship-b/w-Entities****
Topic - Broker = M:1
Subscription - Broker = M:1
Publisher - Broker = M:1
Subscriber - Broker = M:1
Message - Topic = M:1
Topic - Subscriber = M:M
Topic - Publisher = M:M

****Design-Patterns****
Observer Design Pattern and Facade Desing Pattern
Broker is the Facade and Observer subject
Subscriber is the Observer





Step-5: Schema Design + Attributes (PK + FK + attrib) + Cardinalities

****Cardinalities****
Topic - Broker = M:1
Publisher - Broker = M:1
Subscriber - Broker = M:1
Message - Topic = M:1
Topic - Subscriber = M:M
Topic - Publisher = M:M
Subscription - Subscriber = M:1
Subscription - Topic = M:1

****Schema Desgin + Attributes (PK + FK + attrib) ****

Topic(id String [Primary key], String name, latestOffset long, broker_id String [Foreign Key])

Broker(id String PK, String name)

Publisher(id String PK, String name, broker_id String [Foreign key])

Subscriber(id String PK, String name, broker_id String [Foreign key])

Message(id String PK, String payload, offset long, String topic_id [Foreign Key])

Topic_Publisher_lookUp(topic_id String, publisher_id String, [Primary key(topic_id, publisher_id)])

Topic_Subscription(topic_id String, subscriber_id String, lastCommitedOffset long, [Primary Key(topic_id, subscriber_id)])

